1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:01,477
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:02,950
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,973 --> 00:00:05,090
This has to stay...

4
00:00:05,523 --> 00:00:06,949
absolutely secret.

5
00:00:07,851 --> 00:00:08,851
Promise me.

6
00:00:09,615 --> 00:00:10,923
My goodness.

7
00:00:11,961 --> 00:00:13,860
You didn't know either?

8
00:00:13,906 --> 00:00:16,947
I never imagined it.
You didn't either, right?

9
00:00:17,426 --> 00:00:20,386
Even after going there and begging,
she wouldn't even do a blood test.

10
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,603
That girl is incredibly thoughtful.

11
00:00:23,805 --> 00:00:25,908
She asked for it
to be kept completely secret.

12
00:00:26,921 --> 00:00:28,796
Dr. Hwang helped her.

13
00:00:28,798 --> 00:00:30,513
Otherwise, what could we have done?

14
00:00:30,853 --> 00:00:33,510
It's not something we can just exchange
among ourselves.

15
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:38,054
- We owe her a huge debt.
- We really do.

16
00:00:38,445 --> 00:00:40,893
She's such a kind girl.

17
00:00:42,011 --> 00:00:44,420
I feel so sorry, and so grateful.

18
00:00:44,457 --> 00:00:46,119
Just don't make it obvious.

19
00:00:46,209 --> 00:00:48,274
If her mom finds out, she'll be furious.

20
00:00:48,672 --> 00:00:52,139
I basically acted like a spy today
just to deliver the food to her.

21
00:00:52,251 --> 00:00:54,525
Yes, we need to be careful.

22
00:00:54,605 --> 00:00:57,920
When you're truly worn out,
they say you're completely drained,

23
00:00:57,923 --> 00:00:59,603
like it wears you down to the bone.

24
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:02,448
I'm worried that because of this,

25
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:06,387
the girl might have issues
with her health.

26
00:01:16,752 --> 00:01:19,067
There was soy milk broth in the fridge.
Where'd it come from?

27
00:01:19,089 --> 00:01:20,511
That? Jung A gave it to me.

28
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:23,679
Ask her where she got it. It was good.

29
00:01:23,830 --> 00:01:26,121
Not Jung A, her mom gave it.

30
00:01:26,163 --> 00:01:27,914
Her mom's a great cook.

31
00:01:27,948 --> 00:01:31,788
Actually, her mom got it from a friend,
and Jung A gave it to me.

32
00:01:31,872 --> 00:01:34,201
She gave it to me, and I had some left,

33
00:01:34,226 --> 00:01:35,900
- so I put it in the fridge.
- My goodness,

34
00:01:36,062 --> 00:01:38,089
it really made its way here.

35
00:01:38,710 --> 00:01:41,013
- Should I try making it too?
- You?

36
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:42,384
What's so hard about it?

37
00:01:42,386 --> 00:01:43,929
Don't you just need soybeans?

38
00:01:43,932 --> 00:01:45,906
Your grandma used to make it.

39
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:48,327
That's true.

40
00:01:49,485 --> 00:01:52,386
But are you jet-lagged?
You look like you didn't sleep.

41
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:54,088
Right?

42
00:01:54,304 --> 00:01:57,994
I had a really unsettling dream
and woke up at dawn.

43
00:01:58,079 --> 00:02:00,398
- What kind of dream?
- Well, it was...

44
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,236
Never mind. You don't need to know.

45
00:02:17,295 --> 00:02:18,714
Eat up, everyone.

46
00:02:25,485 --> 00:02:26,752
Is it good?

47
00:02:36,436 --> 00:02:38,194
- Se Ri!
- You...

48
00:03:00,003 --> 00:03:01,722
What a messed-up dream.

49
00:03:01,732 --> 00:03:03,687
I was finally starting to feel relieved
because the kid survived,

50
00:03:03,689 --> 00:03:05,109
and then I have a dream like that.

51
00:03:06,015 --> 00:03:08,453
Anyway, I shouldn't think about Seo Chon.

52
00:03:17,325 --> 00:03:18,502
Yes, Counselor.

53
00:03:18,845 --> 00:03:21,374
I'm on my way to the bank now.

54
00:03:23,055 --> 00:03:25,989
Of course I'll invest. Yes.

55
00:03:25,992 --> 00:03:27,419
Don't worry.

56
00:03:28,356 --> 00:03:29,749
I'll see you later.

57
00:03:33,396 --> 00:03:35,453
- Excuse me.
- Yes.

58
00:03:37,283 --> 00:03:39,125
We didn't order delivery.

59
00:03:40,415 --> 00:03:41,582
We didn't order anything.

60
00:03:44,062 --> 00:03:46,387
- Are you Na Ji Ni?
- Yes, that's me.

61
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:49,418
This delivery is for you. Have a good day.

62
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:53,510
What is this?

63
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:01,905
Hello? Who is this?

64
00:04:02,517 --> 00:04:04,996
I'm O Reum's mother.

65
00:04:05,635 --> 00:04:06,871
You're surprised, right?

66
00:04:06,874 --> 00:04:09,708
I'm truly sorry, and grateful.

67
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:12,946
I feel bad
that I can only thank you like this.

68
00:04:14,182 --> 00:04:16,935
If there's anything you want to eat,
have, or do,

69
00:04:16,937 --> 00:04:18,712
just tell me.

70
00:04:18,874 --> 00:04:21,471
I'll do everything I can.

71
00:04:22,335 --> 00:04:23,572
You really didn't have to do this.

72
00:04:23,574 --> 00:04:25,940
That's not why I did it.

73
00:04:26,087 --> 00:04:28,827
I know, thank you.

74
00:04:29,577 --> 00:04:31,756
O Reum wants to see you.

75
00:04:32,002 --> 00:04:33,675
Could you come to the hospital?

76
00:04:34,092 --> 00:04:35,854
You can just see him from afar.

77
00:04:36,116 --> 00:04:38,094
Or should I send a video instead?

78
00:04:38,693 --> 00:04:40,925
Okay...

79
00:04:44,748 --> 00:04:47,882
It's O Reum's mother. This is a problem.

80
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:50,377
The secret keeps leaking,
and it's making me nervous.

81
00:04:50,946 --> 00:04:53,288
Don't worry. It won't go beyond this.

82
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,636
Won't the family eventually find out?

83
00:04:55,872 --> 00:04:57,522
As long as your mom doesn't, it's fine.

84
00:04:58,706 --> 00:05:00,495
How are we supposed to eat all of this?

85
00:05:02,041 --> 00:05:03,041
Here.

86
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:06,899
Support request already submitted.
Don't worry.

87
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:08,554
Thanks to you,

88
00:05:08,592 --> 00:05:10,546
we even went on a planning retreat,

89
00:05:10,669 --> 00:05:12,206
so I think we've earned the right
to eat this.

90
00:05:16,091 --> 00:05:17,847
Thanks to you, we had a great lunch.

91
00:05:19,572 --> 00:05:21,709
I heard the child's mother
is some kind of Vietnamese tycoon.

92
00:05:21,711 --> 00:05:23,333
She really is on a whole different level.

93
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,462
Five of us ate
and there's still food left.

94
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:28,703
Exactly. I really shouldn't accept this.

95
00:05:29,253 --> 00:05:30,972
Just accept it.

96
00:05:31,332 --> 00:05:33,590
If you give someone something so valuable
and get nothing in return,

97
00:05:33,592 --> 00:05:35,360
they end up feeling too indebted.

98
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:39,502
That's true, but my situation is a bit...

99
00:05:40,152 --> 00:05:41,504
Because of your mom, right?

100
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,426
Yes.

101
00:05:43,826 --> 00:05:46,500
Your mom will come
to understand your sincerity.

102
00:05:48,095 --> 00:05:51,410
I don't think sincerity
is always a good thing.

103
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:54,879
Depending on the situation,

104
00:05:55,217 --> 00:05:57,977
even sincerity can feel like violence.

105
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,329
I think about that all the time too.

106
00:06:04,331 --> 00:06:06,343
Everyone says sincerity is a good thing.

107
00:06:07,089 --> 00:06:08,171
That's true.

108
00:06:08,247 --> 00:06:11,446
But I think sincerity has a dark side too.

109
00:06:12,386 --> 00:06:14,073
A dark side of sincerity?

110
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,574
Back in high school,

111
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:20,404
there were things people did sincerely,
but to me, they felt like violence.

112
00:06:22,152 --> 00:06:24,574
Since then, I've developed
a kind of trauma...

113
00:06:24,798 --> 00:06:26,192
around people's sincerity.

114
00:06:31,744 --> 00:06:33,092
I think we've come too far.

115
00:06:33,144 --> 00:06:35,228
- Should we head back?
- Yeah.

116
00:06:36,377 --> 00:06:37,918
Why don't you date, Ji Ni?

117
00:06:39,988 --> 00:06:41,460
There's no special reason.

118
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:44,665
I just don't like relationships
like my dad's,

119
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:47,085
or like my mom's.

120
00:06:47,772 --> 00:06:49,468
Then what about a relationship like yours?

121
00:06:53,506 --> 00:06:55,040
If I ever figure that out,
I'll let you know.

122
00:06:56,512 --> 00:06:57,775
I'll look forward to it.

123
00:07:03,388 --> 00:07:05,693
You didn't have to get me a gift too.

124
00:07:06,554 --> 00:07:08,678
You were the first person I thought of.

125
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:12,492
I'm honored. I'll gratefully accept it.

126
00:07:14,296 --> 00:07:16,574
But I thought you'd be late
because of the bank.

127
00:07:16,576 --> 00:07:18,159
It wrapped up quickly.

128
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:21,026
The collateral was solid,
so the loan got approved fast.

129
00:07:21,102 --> 00:07:24,048
- A loan?
- Yeah, a mortgage loan...

130
00:07:25,068 --> 00:07:26,398
This is a secret.

131
00:07:26,491 --> 00:07:28,212
Especially from Ji Ni.

132
00:07:29,026 --> 00:07:30,512
Well, then.

133
00:07:30,672 --> 00:07:33,362
I've become the keeper
of mother-daughter secrets.

134
00:07:33,550 --> 00:07:36,356
Does Ji Ni have a secret too?

135
00:07:38,036 --> 00:07:40,306
No, nothing like that...

136
00:07:41,363 --> 00:07:42,954
Is this about the Indonesia business?

137
00:07:43,384 --> 00:07:44,693
Yes.

138
00:07:45,370 --> 00:07:48,427
When I went there this time,
it was incredible.

139
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:50,500
But risking your home is going too far.

140
00:07:50,676 --> 00:07:52,332
It wasn't just me.

141
00:07:52,334 --> 00:07:54,846
The lawyer who went with me
got on board first.

142
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:56,965
He said he'd retire
and live off the returns.

143
00:07:57,192 --> 00:08:00,861
That made me want to do it too.

144
00:08:01,434 --> 00:08:04,210
- Would you like to invest too?
- No.

145
00:08:04,595 --> 00:08:07,799
I'd settle for a bigger allowance.

146
00:08:09,132 --> 00:08:13,196
My husband probably talked
to people like that too, right?

147
00:08:13,283 --> 00:08:14,669
It reminds you of him, doesn't it?

148
00:08:15,758 --> 00:08:16,887
I miss him.

149
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:24,297
- I should go. You're busy.
- Okay.

150
00:08:24,372 --> 00:08:26,128
- I'll just see you off here.
- Okay.

151
00:08:52,394 --> 00:08:53,586
(Pediatrics)

152
00:09:16,828 --> 00:09:19,887
I'm sorry you came this far
and barely got to see O Reum.

153
00:09:19,906 --> 00:09:22,318
No, I'm glad I got to see him,
even from afar.

154
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:26,475
You don't have to do all this.

155
00:09:26,478 --> 00:09:29,847
- We're just so grateful.
- Really, it's okay.

156
00:09:29,892 --> 00:09:33,873
I'll visit O Reum
when he's out of isolation.

157
00:09:33,961 --> 00:09:35,198
Okay.

158
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:47,752
Ji Ni.

159
00:09:49,055 --> 00:09:50,798
Mom...

160
00:09:56,542 --> 00:09:57,638
Se Ri.

161
00:09:58,234 --> 00:10:00,821
- We were just...
- We?

162
00:10:01,889 --> 00:10:03,111
We?

163
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:27,931
- Mom!
- Se Ri!

164
00:10:27,969 --> 00:10:29,380
- Mom, I'm sorry, Mom.
- Doctor!

165
00:10:29,419 --> 00:10:31,294
- Doctor!
- Mom, wake up!

166
00:10:31,337 --> 00:10:33,461
Mai, get a doctor!

167
00:10:34,407 --> 00:10:36,752
Mom!

168
00:10:37,694 --> 00:10:39,294
Get up. Are you okay?

169
00:10:39,321 --> 00:10:41,890
Let go. I'm fine. Let go.

170
00:10:43,485 --> 00:10:46,053
- Mom.
- I said let go!

171
00:10:52,154 --> 00:10:54,542
- Mom.
- Don't follow me!

172
00:10:55,017 --> 00:10:56,175
Don't follow me.

173
00:10:59,351 --> 00:11:01,031
I said don't follow me!

174
00:11:06,797 --> 00:11:08,041
Mom!

175
00:11:09,287 --> 00:11:12,310
- Mom!
- Ma'am, are you okay? Wake up.

176
00:11:12,365 --> 00:11:14,148
- Mom!
- Can you hear me?

177
00:11:14,230 --> 00:11:17,940
- What do I do? Mom...
- Ma'am, wake up.

178
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:38,272
- Please don't come.
- But...

179
00:11:38,702 --> 00:11:40,491
This is something
mom and I should resolve.

180
00:11:48,175 --> 00:11:51,544
Mom.

181
00:11:52,041 --> 00:11:53,869
- Mom, are you okay?
- Se Ri.

182
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,384
Are you awake?

183
00:12:02,542 --> 00:12:03,711
Mom...

184
00:12:04,966 --> 00:12:05,966
Are you okay?

185
00:12:12,706 --> 00:12:14,222
Mom, no!

186
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:17,620
Mom.

187
00:12:39,506 --> 00:12:41,886
Please go. I'll call you later.

188
00:12:42,925 --> 00:12:44,659
Mom!

189
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:55,729
Mom!

190
00:12:57,337 --> 00:12:58,605
Mom!

191
00:13:00,850 --> 00:13:04,137
Mom!

192
00:13:05,111 --> 00:13:06,340
Mom!

193
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,086
Mom, please open the door. Mom.

194
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:14,613
Mom!

195
00:13:15,851 --> 00:13:17,044
Mom.

196
00:14:08,004 --> 00:14:09,557
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

197
00:14:15,719 --> 00:14:17,719
(Stem Cell Donation Certificate)

198
00:14:48,148 --> 00:14:50,713
What if she sets our house on fire?

199
00:14:53,437 --> 00:14:55,063
What? You saw her earlier.

200
00:14:55,065 --> 00:14:56,940
She was completely unstable.

201
00:14:57,190 --> 00:14:59,565
Mom, today isn't the right time,

202
00:15:00,106 --> 00:15:03,481
but I should visit
and apologize to her tomorrow.

203
00:15:03,981 --> 00:15:05,582
Would she even accept that?

204
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:08,546
I have no idea how to handle this.

205
00:15:08,731 --> 00:15:10,187
I can't think straight.

206
00:15:10,190 --> 00:15:13,109
She was so cold to Ji Ni earlier.

207
00:15:13,898 --> 00:15:16,381
What if she beats Ji Ni to death?

208
00:15:19,315 --> 00:15:20,521
Why do you keep hitting me?

209
00:15:20,523 --> 00:15:22,455
I'm serious. It could really happen.

210
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:26,063
Shouldn't we go take the beating instead?

211
00:15:26,065 --> 00:15:28,479
You go and take it until she calms down.

212
00:15:28,481 --> 00:15:30,217
If that would help, I'd do it.

213
00:15:41,898 --> 00:15:42,898
Mom.

214
00:15:43,658 --> 00:15:44,658
Mom?

215
00:15:45,981 --> 00:15:47,815
So it's Mom now?

216
00:15:47,981 --> 00:15:51,773
If I were your mom,
you couldn't do this to me.

217
00:15:51,815 --> 00:15:55,313
I was against it
and said no countless times,

218
00:15:55,315 --> 00:15:57,712
but you still made a fool out of me?

219
00:15:58,731 --> 00:16:00,466
Go live with that family.

220
00:16:00,481 --> 00:16:03,063
If you care so much about them,
go live with them.

221
00:16:03,065 --> 00:16:04,690
That's not what this is.

222
00:16:04,981 --> 00:16:06,771
And where would I go?

223
00:16:06,773 --> 00:16:08,271
I'm Na Ji Ni, Na Se Ri's daughter.

224
00:16:08,273 --> 00:16:10,108
Then go and be Cha Ji Ni now.

225
00:16:10,398 --> 00:16:12,940
They'll welcome you now.
They'll be overjoyed.

226
00:16:12,981 --> 00:16:14,773
Please stop this.

227
00:16:15,731 --> 00:16:17,816
- I know how you feel, Mom.
- What do you know?

228
00:16:17,819 --> 00:16:19,015
If you knew, would you do this?

229
00:16:19,017 --> 00:16:23,193
You betrayed your own mother
and even made me pass out?

230
00:16:24,523 --> 00:16:26,663
If you were so desperate
to belong to that family,

231
00:16:26,665 --> 00:16:29,625
how did you manage
to stay by my side until now?

232
00:16:30,731 --> 00:16:32,563
Go. You leave too.

233
00:16:32,565 --> 00:16:34,860
Who said I was going anywhere?

234
00:16:35,326 --> 00:16:37,070
Dad, Mom, and me. We're a family of three.

235
00:16:37,072 --> 00:16:38,479
Stop talking nonsense.

236
00:16:38,481 --> 00:16:40,625
Maybe your dad wanted to leave too.

237
00:16:41,864 --> 00:16:44,066
Go and be Cha Ji Ni too.

238
00:16:46,481 --> 00:16:51,356
You deceived me
and smiled with that family?

239
00:16:51,523 --> 00:16:54,356
I can't believe this. Honestly.

240
00:16:54,731 --> 00:16:57,106
Na Se Ri.

241
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:00,002
What have you been doing with your life?

242
00:17:06,773 --> 00:17:08,854
Out of guilt for not
letting you call me Mom,

243
00:17:08,856 --> 00:17:13,315
I played cello until my fingers wore down
to raise you to be the best.

244
00:17:14,148 --> 00:17:16,481
What was it all for?

245
00:17:20,815 --> 00:17:23,690
Mom, please stop.

246
00:17:24,356 --> 00:17:26,606
I just wanted to save him.

247
00:17:27,445 --> 00:17:30,695
He was dying through no fault
of his own, just like I was.

248
00:17:31,148 --> 00:17:33,699
I just couldn't turn away from him.

249
00:17:34,731 --> 00:17:37,023
I didn't mean to betray you, Mom.

250
00:17:37,231 --> 00:17:40,065
You watched me dying too, Mom.

251
00:17:43,565 --> 00:17:45,919
Did I say I'd go live with them?

252
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:48,398
Did I say I liked that woman?

253
00:17:49,898 --> 00:17:54,448
Just like you, I struggle too...

254
00:17:54,481 --> 00:17:56,470
when I think of her.

255
00:17:56,815 --> 00:17:59,857
Then why did you do it?

256
00:18:00,398 --> 00:18:02,727
What did it matter to you
whether he lived or died?

257
00:18:02,729 --> 00:18:05,875
You even donated your bone marrow,
you foolish girl!

258
00:18:06,565 --> 00:18:08,854
And then you acted like that
around those people?

259
00:18:08,856 --> 00:18:10,596
You make my blood boil!

260
00:18:11,595 --> 00:18:12,709
It's just...

261
00:18:13,322 --> 00:18:18,110
He can be saved.

262
00:18:18,608 --> 00:18:23,448
If I donate, he'll live. How can I not?

263
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:32,440
Mom, please try to understand.

264
00:18:33,190 --> 00:18:35,815
Your dad said the same thing.
He begged me to understand,

265
00:18:36,106 --> 00:18:38,085
so he could attend
his dad's memorial service.

266
00:18:39,197 --> 00:18:42,399
This isn't the same. I'm different.

267
00:18:44,065 --> 00:18:46,831
Enough. I'm sick of this.

268
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:50,676
Where do you think you're going like this?

269
00:18:59,231 --> 00:19:00,595
Dad,

270
00:19:01,315 --> 00:19:03,612
please talk to her.

271
00:19:04,273 --> 00:19:06,214
She'll listen to you.

272
00:19:07,956 --> 00:19:09,898
Dad.

273
00:19:25,815 --> 00:19:27,106
No Yeong Ju.

274
00:19:38,565 --> 00:19:42,033
I was so worried, I couldn't stay home.

275
00:19:42,606 --> 00:19:44,060
We had no idea.

276
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,398
Ji Ni...

277
00:19:46,273 --> 00:19:48,172
Your daughter is so thoughtful.

278
00:19:48,565 --> 00:19:50,572
She tried to keep it from us.

279
00:19:51,174 --> 00:19:53,241
But I found out anyway.

280
00:19:56,464 --> 00:19:59,341
None of it matters anymore. It's over.

281
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:02,011
It all feels so pointless.

282
00:20:02,013 --> 00:20:04,395
I just want to give up.

283
00:20:05,272 --> 00:20:06,481
I'm exhausted.

284
00:20:07,097 --> 00:20:09,864
Don't say that, Se Ri.

285
00:20:10,690 --> 00:20:11,868
I truly...

286
00:20:13,148 --> 00:20:16,212
want to apologize
for everything I did to you.

287
00:20:18,231 --> 00:20:20,085
Before, you only apologized
because you had to.

288
00:20:21,273 --> 00:20:22,622
You're right.

289
00:20:23,898 --> 00:20:26,190
I thought I had it worse.

290
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:28,693
So now you think we're even?

291
00:20:29,398 --> 00:20:30,935
No.

292
00:20:31,357 --> 00:20:35,006
Now, regardless of the past,

293
00:20:35,523 --> 00:20:38,688
I just feel grateful and sorry.

294
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:39,901
I really mean it.

295
00:20:44,829 --> 00:20:46,523
Life's funny.

296
00:20:47,981 --> 00:20:49,393
I begged you...

297
00:20:50,111 --> 00:20:53,681
to at least let Ji Ni
live openly with the family name.

298
00:20:54,497 --> 00:20:56,521
I begged you so many times.

299
00:21:00,648 --> 00:21:01,931
Se Ri.

300
00:21:04,606 --> 00:21:06,481
It's so unfair.

301
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:11,574
You should've done this back then.

302
00:21:12,690 --> 00:21:14,935
You should've at least
let the girl have a life.

303
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:20,189
She was kind enough
to donate her bone marrow.

304
00:21:20,981 --> 00:21:23,141
She's still part of that family.

305
00:21:27,731 --> 00:21:30,122
I just can't forgive you...

306
00:21:30,432 --> 00:21:32,687
for acting like this now.

307
00:21:33,106 --> 00:21:35,648
It's driving me crazy.

308
00:21:36,065 --> 00:21:40,190
Yeah. I know how you feel.
This is all my fault.

309
00:21:41,114 --> 00:21:43,203
I shouldn't have treated her that way.

310
00:21:43,606 --> 00:21:46,520
I was young back then too.

311
00:21:47,398 --> 00:21:49,760
I think I was only focused on my own pain.

312
00:21:50,148 --> 00:21:51,601
I'm really sorry.

313
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:59,483
I should've died back then.

314
00:21:59,856 --> 00:22:01,439
Then I wouldn't have to see this.

315
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:05,893
I should've given up and died back then.

316
00:22:06,565 --> 00:22:09,137
When my mom told me to go out and die,

317
00:22:10,031 --> 00:22:12,189
I should've really done it.

318
00:22:13,523 --> 00:22:17,310
I thought I was loving someone
with my whole world at stake,

319
00:22:19,148 --> 00:22:20,622
but it all feels so meaningless now.

320
00:22:28,898 --> 00:22:29,989
Where are you going?

321
00:22:30,132 --> 00:22:32,606
I don't think you should go out right now.

322
00:22:32,731 --> 00:22:33,938
Go inside.

323
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:35,898
I'll make you something.

324
00:22:36,356 --> 00:22:37,539
Forget it.

325
00:22:42,498 --> 00:22:45,104
Did you make soy milk broth for Ji Ni?

326
00:22:45,981 --> 00:22:47,190
What?

327
00:22:47,773 --> 00:22:49,862
Well, that...

328
00:22:57,966 --> 00:22:59,539
Life is strange.

329
00:24:16,648 --> 00:24:19,568
Yeong Ju, stay strong.

330
00:24:20,057 --> 00:24:23,137
It'll be okay. She's still her daughter.

331
00:24:23,606 --> 00:24:24,879
She's still her mother.

332
00:24:26,690 --> 00:24:29,531
They say mothers and daughters
fight a lot,

333
00:24:29,690 --> 00:24:31,565
but they always work it out.

334
00:24:33,481 --> 00:24:37,690
Maybe Se Ri is still angry
because of all the pain...

335
00:24:38,648 --> 00:24:41,818
she endured from me all these years.

336
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:44,856
That's not it.

337
00:24:45,398 --> 00:24:47,101
She was the one who started this.

338
00:24:48,039 --> 00:24:49,508
You're the one who got hurt.

339
00:24:50,398 --> 00:24:51,981
Let's not talk about us.

340
00:24:53,065 --> 00:24:54,815
We did things...

341
00:24:55,606 --> 00:24:57,690
to innocent children
that we never should've done.

342
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:02,895
Even though we're family,
I turned my back on them.

343
00:25:06,231 --> 00:25:07,874
Don't dwell on it.

344
00:25:08,231 --> 00:25:09,383
Back then,

345
00:25:10,059 --> 00:25:12,093
we were all so angry.

346
00:25:18,606 --> 00:25:20,476
He's the only one
who got to die and be at peace.

347
00:25:20,815 --> 00:25:23,315
Everything happened because of him.

348
00:25:24,065 --> 00:25:26,065
He was selfish until the very end.

349
00:25:55,132 --> 00:25:56,132
Se Ri.

350
00:25:57,106 --> 00:25:59,876
You're here, Sa Bin.

351
00:26:00,190 --> 00:26:01,523
My dear Sa Bin.

352
00:26:02,190 --> 00:26:04,822
Have a drink with me.

353
00:26:06,338 --> 00:26:08,593
Today...

354
00:26:08,811 --> 00:26:11,268
I'm going to drink until I pass out.

355
00:26:11,773 --> 00:26:12,940
Is that okay?

356
00:26:13,331 --> 00:26:14,581
Did something happen?

357
00:26:18,481 --> 00:26:19,566
"Did something happen?"

358
00:26:22,023 --> 00:26:24,483
My life is one disaster after another.

359
00:26:25,556 --> 00:26:27,306
My life is a minefield.

360
00:26:28,123 --> 00:26:31,526
Ever since I met that Cha Min Ki,

361
00:26:32,106 --> 00:26:34,214
my life has been a minefield every day.

362
00:26:36,190 --> 00:26:37,771
Drink slowly.

363
00:26:37,773 --> 00:26:40,579
Have some food with it too.

364
00:26:41,190 --> 00:26:42,345
Sa Bin.

365
00:26:43,565 --> 00:26:45,183
I got hit by a bomb today.

366
00:26:50,148 --> 00:26:51,898
My life was blown away.

367
00:26:52,731 --> 00:26:54,654
There's nothing left.

368
00:26:56,565 --> 00:26:58,106
I don't understand a thing you're saying.

369
00:26:58,231 --> 00:27:00,991
You don't understand any of it, right?

370
00:27:03,606 --> 00:27:05,329
Honestly, I don't either.

371
00:27:08,981 --> 00:27:10,166
I feel so empty.

372
00:27:12,981 --> 00:27:15,385
I really want to die.

373
00:27:15,773 --> 00:27:17,168
I'm losing my mind.

374
00:27:48,731 --> 00:27:52,023
(Family Register)

375
00:27:52,148 --> 00:27:53,357
If you could forgive me,

376
00:27:53,359 --> 00:27:55,146
I'd do anything to thank you.

377
00:27:55,148 --> 00:27:56,815
Then give me the Seo Chon house.

378
00:27:56,856 --> 00:27:58,063
The one in Seo Chon?

379
00:27:58,065 --> 00:27:59,690
Were you just going to give me some money
and be done with it?

380
00:27:59,731 --> 00:28:02,146
Do Hee and I have been struggling lately.
You know that, right?

381
00:28:02,148 --> 00:28:03,271
That happens.

382
00:28:03,273 --> 00:28:04,688
I guess it's not that passionate.

383
00:28:04,690 --> 00:28:05,997
Do Hee must be worried sick.

384
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,034
My sweet daughter.

385
00:28:07,036 --> 00:28:10,271
I'm sorry you suffered so much
because of a mother like me.

386
00:28:10,273 --> 00:28:12,396
How can you live your whole life
thinking only of yourself?

387
00:28:12,398 --> 00:28:14,898
If you leave like this,
how am I supposed to go on living?

388
00:28:15,691 --> 00:28:17,820
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
